Z||000000||The Dealer||06-19-2001||06:18 PM||||hey everyone,<P>I'm new to this board and I am going to purchase an 86 Fiero SE soon with a 2.8 V6 and a 4spd manaul.  The current owner tells me that he just put in new headlight motors, but the passenger side relay needs to be replaced..  Anyone have experience on that?<P>The Dealer||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrgone||06-19-2001||08:25 PM||||welcome to the forum, i reccomend you get the car checked out by a reputable mechanic to avoid any surprizes <P>popup headlights tend to do that<P>do a search on a keyword if you have any questions||||reg||1
Z||000002||84Bill||06-19-2001||10:24 PM||||Welcome to the Forum  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>There are 2 sets of relays next to each headlight mount bracket. You could go to a yard and get them for fairly cheep (under 10 bucks a pair) or I can send you one if you want, just pay me for the shipping.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000003||The Dealer||06-19-2001||11:49 PM||||84Bill,<P>That sounds like a feasible option, I will let you know for sure once I have the car and I know it needs to be replaced, Thanks,<P>The Dealer||||reg||1
Z||000004||StuGood||06-20-2001||08:06 AM||||At the risk of telling you what you already know... a simple way of determining if a headlight relay is at fault, is to swap the headlight-motor relays (from one headlight motor to the other and vice-versa).  A fairly easy test. If the problem swaps sides (with the relays), then it's obvious you just need to replace the bad relay, as the seller claims.  <P>If the problem doesn't travel along with the relay, you will probably have to rebuild the headlight motors... a more time-consuming, but still rewarding, task.        ||||reg||3
Z||000005||The Dealer||06-20-2001||11:56 AM||||StuGod,<P>In the opening post, I mentioned that the headlight motors were just replaced by the current owner, and he has informed me that the relay needs to be replaced.  The testing procedure you mentioned will be how I will test the motors.<P>Thanks,<P>The Dealer||||reg||1
